The Lord said to him,
“Arise, and go to the street which is called Straight, and inquire in the house of Judah
for one named Saul, a man of Tarsus. For behold, he is praying,

‘Behold, you scoffers, and wonder, and perish;
for I work a work in your days,
a work which you will in no way believe, if one declares it to you.’”

That the rest of men may seek after the Lord;
all the Gentiles who are called by my name,
says the Lord, who does all these things.

He said to them,
“What things?”
They said to him, “The things concerning Jesus, the Nazarene, who was a prophet mighty in deed and word before God and all the people;

They said to him, “We are able.”
Jesus said to them,
“You shall indeed drink the cup that I drink, and you shall be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with;

for this people’s heart has grown callous,
their ears are dull of hearing,
they have closed their eyes;
or else perhaps they might perceive with their eyes,
hear with their ears,
understand with their heart,
and would turn again;
and I would heal them.’

that it might be fulfilled which was spoken through the prophet, saying,
“I will open my mouth in parables;
I will utter things hidden from the foundation of the world.”

‘These people draw near to me with their mouth,
and honor me with their lips;
but their heart is far from me.
